  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/... \nThe benign weather conditions will continue to prevail well into\nnext week with the lingering trough finally moving out of the\nregion on Sunday and being replaced by weak ridging to zonal\nwesterly flow. This pattern shift will lead to continued mostly\nclear skies and dry conditions, while allowing temperatures to\ngradually warm back into the normal range by the middle of next\nweek. Expect the bulk of the lower deserts to have daily highs in\nthe low to possibly mid 80s and lows from the mid 50s to mid 60s\nduring the first half of next week. Model uncertainty comes into \nplay later next week as there are hints at some moisture return\ninto the region out of the southeast and then a potential \natmospheric river approaching by next weekend. Either or both of \nthese moisture sources may eventually help to bring a return to \nrain chances at some point before the end of the month, but it is \ntoo early to have a good idea on timing and/or placement for any \nweather systems over a week out.",
